8:["$","div",null,{"className":"animate-rise-in pointer-events-auto mt-6 sm:mt-8","style":{"animationDelay":"480ms"},"children":["$","$L11",null,{"items":[{"quote":"In the ICU the question is never just calories — it's protein the gut will actually tolerate. Having a 100% whey, high-protein option has changed how early we can start feeding.","name":"Clinical Dietitian","meta":"Intensive Care Unit · Tertiary hospital, Kathmandu","kind":"clinician","quoteKey":"col:testimonials.0.quote","nameKey":"col:testimonials.0.name"},{"quote":"Renal patients need restraint as much as nutrition. A low-protein formula with the electrolyte profile printed plainly makes the prescribing conversation much simpler.","name":"Consultant Nephrologist","meta":"Renal Unit · Kathmandu","kind":"clinician","quoteKey":"col:testimonials.1.quote","nameKey":"col:testimonials.1.name"},{"quote":"Glycaemic control and adequate nutrition usually pull in opposite directions. The low-GI formulation lets us stop choosing between them.","name":"Endocrinologist","meta":"Diabetes Clinic · Lalitpur","kind":"clinician","quoteKey":"col:testimonials.2.quote","nameKey":"col:testimonials.2.name"},{"quote":"After Aama's surgery she could barely eat. Two weeks on progain-hp and she was asking for dal bhat again.","name":"Daughter & carer","meta":"Family · Pokhara","kind":"family","quoteKey":"col:testimonials.3.quote","nameKey":"col:testimonials.3.name"},{"quote":"On dialysis you worry about everything you eat. This is one thing I don't have to second-guess.","name":"Dialysis patient","meta":"Patient · Kathmandu","kind":"family","quoteKey":"col:testimonials.4.quote","nameKey":"col:testimonials.4.name"},{"quote":"Buwa's doctor suggested progain-dm. Now breakfast is the one thing on his plate we don't argue about.","name":"Son & carer","meta":"Family · Butwal","kind":"family","quoteKey":"col:testimonials.5.quote","nameKey":"col:testimonials.5.name"}]}]}]
